   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "A thin slab of thickness dh holds about \\( 6.25\\,\\rho(h)\\,dh \\), so the total is \\( 6.25\\int_{2}^{6} \\left(6 \\sin{\\left(\\frac{h^{2}}{4} \\right)} + 30\\right)\\,dh \\).",
         "rule_named": "accumulation of a density"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "With the calculator in radian mode the integral is about 125.560.",
         "mathjson": 125.55953070204465,
         "rule_named": "numerical integration"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Multiplying by the area 6.25 gives about 784.747.",
